* Sorry but I'm not happy about this. Please see [[WP:NOTLAB|"Wikipedia is not a laboratory"]]. The proposal could be regarded as somewhat "disruptive to the community" in diluting the value of the barnstar, which we would hope is intended as a sincere expression of appreciation from one Wikipedia editor to another. Now I wouldn't pretend the proposal is some kind of life-threatening intervention, but by its nature the experiment cannot seek the informed consent of participants and as such does not set a good example. Wikipedia editors are not lab rats and should not be fed barnstars to see if they scurry round any faster afterwards! Feel free to disregard this if other contributors don't see it this way[[User:Noyster|: <b style="color:seagreen">Noyster</b>]] [[User talk:Noyster|<span style="color:seagreen"> (talk),</span> ]] 18:36, 19 December 2018 (UTC)
